   "like_count": 7,
   "cooked": "<p></p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" data-download-href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/be2c08dcd7532f2b89d5abad5d9642d9558562a3\" href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/be2c08dcd7532f2b89d5abad5d9642d9558562a3.jpeg\" title=\"\"><img alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"r8l3UDZBC8AgbvVDGEMTZJv1nGj\" data-small-upload=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/be2c08dcd7532f2b89d5abad5d9642d9558562a3_2_10x10.png\" height=\"244\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/be2c08dcd7532f2b89d5abad5d9642d9558562a3_2_244x244.jpeg\" srcset=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/be2c08dcd7532f2b89d5abad5d9642d9558562a3_2_244x244.jpeg, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/be2c08dcd7532f2b89d5abad5d9642d9558562a3_2_366x366.jpeg 1.5x, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/be2c08dcd7532f2b89d5abad5d9642d9558562a3_2_488x488.jpeg 2x\" width=\"244\"/><div class=\"meta\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\"><use xlink:href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\"></span><span class=\"informations\">1080×1080 319 KB</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\"><use xlink:href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div>\n<p>So we have come to it.</p>\n<p>The TEC Test Hatch DAO was launched and we have a <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/tec-test-hatch-implementation-specification/226\">full implementation specification</a> for it, confirming what parameters and permissions need to be determined by the community to complete the Hatch.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/LinuxIsCool\">@YGG</a> has been leading the effort to create a beautiful cadCAD model to make it easy for anyone (even non-devs) to choose their own Hatch Params holistically, and understand the impact their choices will have.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/tokenlog-token-weighted-backlog/188/9\">Tokenlog</a> from <a href=\"https://twitter.com/wslyvh\">@Wslyv</a> is ready for us to play with and will allow us to vote on the various parameters proposed by the community.</p>\n<p>The main pieces are in place, but the devil is in the details. We need to formally decide exactly how the Hatch Params will be chosen.</p>\n<h2>The Hatch Param Proposal Submission Process</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>We will create videos and forum posts explaining this process in detail.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>We will have a website that uses our cadCAD model to enable you, whether you are a dev or a non-technical user to choose the design Parameters for the TEC Hatch DAO.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Once you are happy with your parameters, you would make an issue in this Github at this <a href=\"https://github.com/TECommons/Token-Log-Hatch-Params\">Github repo</a> with a link to the output of your design. You will want to explain your choices in the github issue.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Once you have made your issue you will want to make note of it in a <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/c/Defi-legos-and-how-they-work-together/tk-log-params/21\">dedicated Forum thread</a> for further discussion.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>What will these <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jrOGGOh-A_Q\">cadCAD models</a> look like?  Here is a sneak peak of the visualization of what it will take to pass a proposal using Dandelion Voting:</p>\n<p></p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" data-download-href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/a06b01482cba656d45cd97474172ba6942281e95\" href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/a06b01482cba656d45cd97474172ba6942281e95.png\" title=\"\"><img alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"mT7ErZtVGe47v6kCPAddG6B0DXv\" data-small-upload=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/a06b01482cba656d45cd97474172ba6942281e95_2_10x10.png\" height=\"232\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/a06b01482cba656d45cd97474172ba6942281e95_2_624x232.png\" srcset=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/a06b01482cba656d45cd97474172ba6942281e95_2_624x232.png, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/a06b01482cba656d45cd97474172ba6942281e95_2_936x348.png 1.5x, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/a06b01482cba656d45cd97474172ba6942281e95.png 2x\" width=\"624\"/><div class=\"meta\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\"><use xlink:href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\"></span><span class=\"informations\">1184×441 45.4 KB</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\"><use xlink:href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div>\n<h2>Voting on the various proposed Hatch Params</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>As a community, we will support <a href=\"https://twitter.com/wslyvh\">@Wslyv</a> in improving <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/tokenlog-token-weighted-backlog/188/9\">Tokenlog</a> for our usecase. He has already made several improvements, for more details check out: <a class=\"inline-onebox\" href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/tokenlog-for-the-prime-time-vote/230\">Tokenlog for the Prime Time Vote</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Any one that has earned CSTK tokens or Impact Hours will be able to vote on the Token Log Repo.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Voting power will be split 50% to CSTK Holders and 50% to Impact Hours</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Voting will be quadratic, as in, to allocate more voting power to your favorite set of Parameters it will take more tokens.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Once everything is set on the cultural and technical sides, A date and time will be chosen by the Community Stewards and the set of parameters with the most votes at moment will be the Parameters we use.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>How does this sound? How can we improve this process?</h3>",
